        /* v14.2 (Wil, 9/16): the films that would not play, the play glyph
           and the soft hero still are iOS Low Power Mode ("I turned off Low
           Power Mode and everything worked as normal"). There play() rejects,
           and until now the rejection was swallowed with the <video> left
           mounted over the still: WebKit draws its play button on a frozen
           first frame, and the still beneath it was the 480px tier, which at
           DPR 3 is what read as low resolution. Wil's decision: PLAY ON FIRST
           TAP. A rejected film is taken out of the box (inline display:none —
           no box, no glyph; inline beats `md:block`), the sibling <picture>'s
           480px sources are removed so the <img> re-selects the 800px still (a
           spec-defined relevant mutation: source selection re-runs with no
           blank frame; the preload links are untouched), and ONE retry is
           armed on the window for the next tap or key. `pointerup`, because a
           pan ends in `pointercancel` — a scroll never spends the retry — and
           Escape is excluded because the spec excludes it from user
           activation. The retry starts every pending film synchronously inside
           the gesture and un-hides each only once its play() resolves. A film
           that carries a poster (the ch2 archival strip) is exempt: there
           WebKit's own tap-to-play over the poster is the right behaviour. */
        const pending = new Set<HTMLVideoElement>();
        let armed = false;
        const retry = (e: Event) => {
          if (e.type === "keydown" && (e as KeyboardEvent).key === "Escape") return;
          window.removeEventListener("pointerup", retry, true);
          window.removeEventListener("keydown", retry, true);
